1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:06,588
Today we continue our series on ecology and conservation with a look at a

2
00:00:06,588 --> 00:00:10,880
particularly endangered member of the black bear family.

3
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:17,043
One in ten black bears is actually born with a white coat which is

4
00:00:17,043 --> 00:00:21,660
the result of a special gene that surfaces in a few.

5
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:25,380
Local people have named it the spirit bear.

6
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:31,371
And according to the legends of these communities, its snowy fur brings with it

7
00:00:31,371 --> 00:00:33,080
a special power.

8
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:39,820
Because of this, it has always been highly regarded by them -so much that

9
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:43,390
they do not speak of seeing it to anyone else.

10
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:48,090
It is their way of protecting it when strangers visit the area.

11
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:51,560
The white bear's habitat is quite interesting.

12
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:58,460
The bear's strong relationship with the old- growth rainforest is a complex one.

13
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:04,967
The white bear relies on the huge centuries-old trees in the forest in many

14
00:01:04,967 --> 00:01:05,610
ways.

15
00:01:05,610 --> 00:01:13,071
For example, the old-growth trees have extremely Iong roots that help prevent erosion of

16
00:01:13,071 --> 00:01:16,420
the soil along the banks of the many fish streams.

17
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:22,702
Keeping these banks intact is important because these streams are home to salmon,

18
00:01:22,702 --> 00:01:24,890
which are the bear's main food source.

19
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:30,860
In return, the bear's feeding habits nurture the forest.

20
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:35,173
As the bears eat the salmon, they discard the skin

21
00:01:35,173 --> 00:01:38,503
and bones in great amounts on the forest floor,

22
00:01:38,503 --> 00:01:40,950
which provide vital nutrients.

23
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:50,586
These produce lush vegetation that sustains thousands of other types of life forms, from birds to insects

24
00:01:50,586 --> 00:01:51,610
and more.

25
00:01:51,610 --> 00:01:58,073
Today, the spirit bear lives off the coast of the province of British Columbia

26
00:01:58,073 --> 00:01:59,920
on a few islands.

27
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:05,880
There is great concern for their survival since it is estimated that less than

28
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:08,890
two hundred of these white bears remain.

29
00:02:08,890 --> 00:02:14,200
The best way to protect them is to make every effort to preserve the

30
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:25,200
delicate balance of their forest environment - in other words, their ecosystem.

31
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:30,610
The greatest threat to the bear's existence is the loss of its habitat.

32
00:02:30,610 --> 00:02:37,014
Over many years, logging companies have stripped the land by cutting down a large

33
00:02:37,014 --> 00:02:38,760
number of trees.

34
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:44,235
In addition, they have built roads which have fractured the areas where the bear

35
00:02:44,235 --> 00:02:45,358
usually feeds,

36
00:02:45,358 --> 00:02:49,490
and many hibernation sites have also been lost.

37
00:02:49,490 --> 00:02:55,355
The logging of the trees along the streams has damaged the places where the

38
00:02:55,355 --> 00:02:56,540
bears fish.

39
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:02,157
To make matters worse, the number of salmon in those streams is declining

40
00:03:02,157 --> 00:03:06,350
because there is no legal limit on fishing at the moment.

41
00:03:06,350 --> 00:03:13,667
All these influences have a negative impact on the spirit bear's very existence,

42
00:03:13,667 --> 00:03:19,561
which is made all the more fragile by the fact that reproduction among these

43
00:03:19,561 --> 00:03:23,390
bears has always been disappointingly low.

44
00:03:23,390 --> 00:03:27,690
And so, what's the situation going forward?

45
00:03:27,690 --> 00:03:36,098
Community organizations, environmental groups and the British Columbia government are now working together on

46
00:03:36,098 --> 00:03:36,780
the problem.

47
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:43,190
The government is now requiring logging companies to adopt a better logging method,

48
00:03:43,190 --> 00:03:45,380
which is a positive step.

49
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:53,284
However, these measures alone may not be sufficient to ensure a healthy population of

50
00:03:53,284 --> 00:03:55,170
the spirit bear in the future.

51
00:03:55,170 --> 00:03:58,381
Other steps also need to be taken.

52
00:03:58,381 --> 00:04:04,566
While it is important to maintain the spirit bear's habitat, there also needs to

53
00:04:04,566 --> 00:04:07,250
be more emphasis on its expansion.

54
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:13,511
The move is justified as it will also create space for other bears that

55
00:04:13,511 --> 00:04:15,300
are losing their homes ...?
